    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), where `YY` is the last two digits of the owner's `registrationDate` year. It's a read-only, server-derived field assigned at owner creation.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern already used for `customerCode`/`namesakeCount`, I touched five layers:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field mapped to a `membership_number` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 assign the membership number after `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are set (the latter defaults to today in `normalizeNewOwner`). Added a `membershipNumber(Owner)` helper computing `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, year % 100)` \u2014 the `%02d` correctly zero-pads years like 2007 \u2192 `07`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `membershipNumber` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into the GET response.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column. The test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema.sql column is required (and I kept all four dialects consistent).\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The build also runs the OpenAPI generator and MapStruct processor, which confirms the new field flows end-to-end from model to DTO. The `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` test \u2014 which reads back `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and asserts `membershipNumber == customerCode + \"-M\" + yy` \u2014 passes.",
